# Witness: the two lane figures written the wrong way round

Both numbers are real and both are in the log; each is simply in the other's column. This is the
likeliest way this table goes wrong - two figures of the same magnitude, two columns apart - and it
is why each figure is checked against its own lane rather than against the set of figures for its
row. A membership check passes this input. The rule fails it twice.

| Measurement | Unit | Candidate | Control | JIT | Native AOT |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `diagnostics-capture` | record | A fully identified diagnostics record | Its minimal form | 100.8870 | 106.1610 |
